    psp-build:bullseye bash -c 'PATH=/work/staging_dir/bin:/work/staging_dir/usr/bin \
    mipsel-linux-uclibc-objdump -d /work/work/out/<dir>/vmlinux'

Model and assumptions (UNVERIFIED, as DESIGN 5.4): 1 instruction per cycle,
CP0 Count at the core clock (220,912,896 Hz), no cache or MMIO latency;
RX FIFO empty at entry, ACK after 20 polls, replies 0x08 5 words, 0x33 and
Nop 2 words, empty-FIFO read 0xFFFF. Counts are executed instructions; a
nullified delay slot is not counted. Scenario state is set directly in
psc_mem (offsets from include/asm-mips/psc.h, checked against the listing:
wd_ctx = psc_mem+0x9f744, t2d_due = psc_mem+0x9f8f0).

Agreement with the implementer's interpreter (IMPLEMENTATION 9.2):
identical for P08 (+75/+482/+557, +208 B), P33 (+560), TICK (+48), WDP
(+1,104), stack (+216 B Nop path, 488 B T2D); WD +925 (pathcount +922),
first Nop +994 (+990): 3-4 instructions apart, scenario state differs
slightly (which word: UNVERIFIED). T2D 205,884 against 228,520: the
panel text is content-dependent (psc_panel_fill 139,575 and
pspClearDcache 1,289 identical). New here: the scheduler hooks, poll
begin/end, the G3-low gap decomposition and the c_in->c_out model.
